---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import OrganizePdf from '@/components/tools/pdf/OrganizePdf.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="organize-pdf">
  <OrganizePdf client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <section>
      <h2>How to reorder pages in a PDF</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Drop the PDF onto the box above. Each page shows as a thumbnail card.</li>
        <li>
          Drag a card to a new position, or use the ◀ and ▶ buttons on the card. The buttons work with
          the keyboard, so the whole tool works without a mouse.
        </li>
        <li>Rotate, duplicate or delete individual pages with the buttons underneath each thumbnail.</li>
        <li>Press <strong>Export PDF</strong> to build the reorganised document and download it.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Deleted pages go to a restore strip and are not discarded. Before you export,
        <strong>Reset</strong> returns the document to its original state at any time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What each control does</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="min-w-[560px]">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Control</th>
              <th scope="col">Effect</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Drag a card / arrow buttons</td>
              <td>Moves the page. All later pages renumber automatically</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Rotate left / right</td>
              <td>Adds 90° to that page's stored rotation, cumulative</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Duplicate</td>
              <td>Inserts a second copy of the page immediately after it</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Delete</td>
              <td>Moves the page to the restore strip, out of the export</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Reverse order</td>
              <td>Reverses the whole document. Useful for back-to-front scans</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Reset</td>
              <td>Restores the original order, rotations and deletions</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        The small grey label under each card (for example <code class="font-mono">p7</code>) is the
        page's number in the original file, so you can always see where a card came from.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Fixing a badly scanned document</h2>
      <p>
        A sheet-feed scanner without duplex gives all the fronts, then all the backs in reverse order.
        To fix it here: scan the fronts, scan the backs, merge the two files, then use this tool to
        interleave them. Drag the last back page after the first front page and work inwards. For a
        small document that takes under a minute. The page content is not rendered again, so nothing
        degrades.
      </p>
      <p>
        Export copies page objects exactly, so you can organise the same PDF many times with no
        generational loss: the tenth export is byte-for-byte as sharp as the first.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Large documents</h2>
      <p>
        Thumbnails render one page at a time, so the interface stays responsive, and a progress bar
        shows the progress. A few hundred pages is fine on a laptop. On a phone, the previews take
        longer and memory is the limit. Nothing is uploaded, so a confidential document stays
        confidential.
      </p>
    </section>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
